{
  "_readme": "The Codex supplement resolve, replayed by BOTH implementations: `codexProvider.ResolveProviderData` in the Go worker and `resolveCodexMessage` in the browser plugin. Codex fills `aggregatedOutput` only on a COMPLETED item, so a turn that ends first leaves the started item with no output and the worker's join is the only copy. A divergence between the two copies draws a retained command row with its output missing and states nothing about why. Each case gives the frame Codex sent, the envelope the worker stored beside it, and the object both sides must produce. The key names come from contracts/codex-protocol.json; these cases pin the BEHAVIOUR the names carry. A second join puts the wait outputs of a code-mode cell on the exec output item that they continue, under the LeapMux key continuationOutputs. The stored row is the whole rawResponseItem/completed frame, so the item is at params.item, or at the top level of a frame without an object at params. A divergence there draws a cell card that lacks the output after its first yield.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "the joined output lands on the item it names",
      "original": {
        "threadId": "thread-1",
        "item": {
          "id": "item-1",
          "type": "commandExecution",
          "command": "ls -1",
          "status": "in_progress"
        }
      },
      "supplemental": {
        "itemId": "item-1",
        "itemType": "commandExecution",
        "aggregatedOutput": "a.go\nb.go\n"
      },
      "expected": {
        "threadId": "thread-1",
        "item": {
          "id": "item-1",
          "type": "commandExecution",
